{"availability":"available","full":"HerringtonDarkholme/hd-lang","name":"hd-lang","description":"My Toy Language","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":32,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-19T04:44:06Z","updated":"2026-10-17T05:08:23Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://herringtondarkholme.github.io/hd-lang/","topics":[],"demo":"https://herringtondarkholme.github.io/hd-lang/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:24.488Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:24.488Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:24.488Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:22.516Z","stars":4,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:47.059Z","stars":99,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:25.388Z","stars":7,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:14:24.488Z","stars":32,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A statically typed, indentation-based language that compiles to WebAssembly, built for code that AI writes and humans review.","Without requirements, a function that sends mail and reads the clock looks like any other, and a test must patch globals or pull in a mocking library to check it. With them, the signature lists what the function touches, and the test installs a fake mailer and a fixed clock for one block. Forgetting a provider is a missing-requirement compile error, not a runtime surprise.","Typed facts and structural derive generate them in plain hd. No macros, no codegen."],"features":["Serialization, schemas, property tests, and fake data from your types.","Effects you can review. A signature shows every capability a function","Sandboxed. Wasm GC, with host access only through requirements."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HerringtonDarkholme/hd-lang/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b9c35b8b578848ba2b968eff9fc275533cdc40180e829689e6c5d288b605a37d","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:47.148Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:25.505Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A statically typed, inde